Subject: [PATCH 2/2] src/lab-process-mail: Leave b/dev to the operator
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: orlxmuxnmznwmyuomlznnzoktqnpurkt
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:31:02 +0000

A pass reads b/dev to see what is coming, and nothing stopped it
from building on what it found there. Work that rests on a b/dev
commit cannot be applied to trunk as posted, and it must be revised
or abandoned whenever Pat rewrites that commit. Saying that such
work waits for trunk keeps every series a contributor posts
applicable to the stable tree. A base other than trunk stays
available for an operator whose own assistant should see the tree
as they do.
